-What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/front-fill-light-test/state
-Date:		September 2026
-Contact:	Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
-Description:
-		Experimental Xiaomi Vince front fill-light diagnostic state.
-		Reports global attempt count, suspend block, logical GPIO
-		readback, fixed on_ms=100/pulses=10 and software_on_us. The
-		timestamp measures software GPIO writes, not physical current
-		or waveform timing. Before firing: attempts=0, level=0.
-		The driver IC/current table and hardware cutoff are unknown.
-
-What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/front-fill-light-test/fire_once
-Date:		September 2026
-Contact:	Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
-Description:
-		Write exactly 1, as root with CAP_SYS_RAWIO, to request the
-		stock ten-pulse front subtorch sequence. A hard hrtimer is
-		armed before the first high and drives low after 100 ms.
-		The request also forces off before returning. Only one attempt
-		per kernel boot, including across unbind/rebind and setup
-		failure. Further requests return EALREADY; during suspend
-		they return EBUSY. No brightness/current/duration selection,
-		automatic trigger or camera-framework integration exists.
-		Probe, managed cleanup, shutdown and suspend force low;
-		resume never restores light or replenishes the attempt.
-		Software timing depends on a functioning CPU and interrupts.
-		It is not a hardware cutoff during a kernel/CPU hang.
